From d0b09a5248723d68ba3bd38ce50af1b29a119dd6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Heinemeier Hansson <david@hey.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 15:46:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add CPPC cpufreq driver

Adds a CPU profile driver for the generic ACPI CPPC cpufreq driver
(cppc_cpufreq) used on ARM64 laptops, which previously only got the
placeholder driver and so had no working profiles at all.

Balanced and power-saver enable CPPC autonomous frequency selection
with an energy performance preference of 64 and 192 respectively.
Performance leaves autonomous selection and runs the performance
governor.

The driver only probes policies that offer both the schedutil and
performance governors and writable autonomous selection knobs. A failed
first activation restores the settings found at probe time, and the
active profile is reapplied on resume in case firmware reset the CPPC
registers.

On an NVIDIA N1X laptop, balanced cut median keystroke-to-frame
latency in Chromium from ~130ms (schedutil) to ~56ms at the same idle
power, and performance to ~32ms.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
